# Build-context upload rules for `gcloud builds submit`.
#
# THIS FILE EXISTS BECAUSE OF A SILENT FAILURE. Without a .gcloudignore, gcloud
# falls back to .gitignore — which excludes `historical/*` as client material.
# The warm transcript cache therefore never reached Cloud Build, the image was
# built with an empty historical/, and the revision aborted at boot with
# `baseline="0/0"`. The image looked fine; the container could not start.
#
# .dockerignore governs the Docker build. This file governs what is uploaded in
# the first place. Both must allow historical/ through, for different reasons.

# Secrets — must never reach a build context.
.env
.env.*
*-service-account*.json

# Client material the runtime does not read.
tmp/
edr_source/
output/
historical_excluded/

# Local build and scratch artifacts.
.git
.gitignore
*.exe
*.exe~
scratch/
docs/

# historical/ is deliberately absent from this list. It carries the warm cache
# the image is built around, and boot refuses to start without it.
